-- title:
--   Integrality over the j-line at j=∞
-- statement:
--   Fix $M\ge 1$ and let $A_M$ denote [`ModularCurve.LevelN.ring M`](def/ModularCurve_LevelNFunctionField.html#L28), the $\mathbb C$-subalgebra of functions $\mathbb H\to\mathbb C$ generated by $j=E_4^3/\Delta$ together with the Fricke functions $\mathrm{fricke}\,M\,v$ for the nonzero $v\in(\mathbb Z/M)^2$. Let $K$ be a field that is simultaneously a $\mathbb C$-algebra and an $A_M$-algebra, compatibly (scalar tower), and a fraction field of $A_M$. Let $\sigma\colon \mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb Z)\to (K\simeq_{\mathbb C} K)$ be a group homomorphism into the $\mathbb C$-algebra automorphisms of $K$ whose kernel is the subgroup generated by $\Gamma(M)$ together with $-1$, and assume the fixed field of the image of $\sigma$ is $\mathbb C$ adjoined the image of $j$ in $K$. Let $E\colon K\to\mathbb C((q))$ be a homomorphism of $\mathbb C$-algebras into Laurent series sending the image of $j$ to $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb C\,M$ applied to $q^{-1}\cdot(E_4^3\eta^{-24})$, i.e. to the $q$-expansion of $j$ with $q$ replaced by $q^M$. Let $z\in K$ be such that for every $\gamma\in\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb Z)$ the Laurent series $E(\sigma_\gamma z)$ has valuation $\le 1$, i.e. no terms of negative order. Then there is a monic $P\in K[X]$ with $P(z)=0$ such that every coefficient $P_i$ can be written as $p(u)/q(u)$ with $p,q\in\mathbb C[X]$, $q(0)\neq0$, where $u$ is the inverse in $K$ of the image of $j$.
--
--   This is the classical statement that an element of the level-$M$ function field whose $q$-expansions at all cusps (equivalently, along all $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb Z)$-translates) have no pole is integral over the local ring $\mathbb C[1/j]_{(1/j)}$ of the $j$-line at $j=\infty$. The monic equation with coefficients of this shape is what is consumed by [`ModularCurve.ord_eq_zero_of_not_mem_of_realizeOf_tendsto`](thm.html#ModularCurve.ord_eq_zero_of_not_mem_of_realizeOf_tendsto) when computing orders at the cusps.
